%% Title: Sequence · the "why?" audit receipt
%% Summary: What happens when a reader opens a post's receipt: the drawer request, the queries behind GET /api/audit/:post_id, the provenance and lineage it adds, and the four audience views the drawer switches between.
%% Sources: public/js/ui.js (openAudit, mapAuditResponse, AUDIENCES), src/routes/audit.js, src/config/{audit-narration,bias-lineage,bias-vocabulary,source-registry,data-mode}.js, src/collectors/retention.js. Spec: TECHNICAL_SPEC.md sections 7 (GET /api/audit/:post_id), 8 (provenance), 10 (explainability chain, audiences).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor Reader
  participant UI as ui.js PulseUI
  participant Main as main.js PulseMain
  participant API as web · GET /api/audit/:post_id
  participant DB as PostgreSQL

  Reader->>UI: click "why?" on a post (city detail or featured post)
  UI->>Main: freezeInsightTimer() (first receipt)
  UI->>UI: open the audit drawer, loading state
  alt demo data on the page, or the post id is not a UUID
    UI->>UI: build the receipt locally (demo), never call the API
  else live post
    UI->>API: GET /api/audit/{post_id}
    API->>API: validate UUID, else 400
    API->>DB: raw_posts JOIN data_sources (content, location, external_id,<br/>provenance_fingerprint, ingest_mv_id, text_removed_at, permalink)
    alt no such post
      API-->>UI: 404 Post not found
    end
    API->>DB: decision_audit_log JOIN methodology_versions for the post
    API->>API: per decision: status, score, 4 audiences rendered from stored<br/>output + config (audit_narration@1.3.0), input_hash as<br/>HMAC-SHA256(AUDIT_HASH_KEY, stored hash), omitted without a key
    API->>DB: bias_assessments of the job that scored the post
    API->>DB: bias methodology versions
    API->>API: bias lineage: recorded (methodology_version_id),<br/>inferred (effective_from), or current, layers from bias@1.1.0 config
    API->>DB: ingest methodology: raw_posts.ingest_mv_id (recorded),<br/>else the version effective at collected_at (inferred)
    API->>API: provenance: source, published_at, permalink unless an identity link,<br/>external_id, fingerprint, how to verify (npm run verify-provenance),<br/>Reddit: retention live (removes_at) or text_removed
    API-->>UI: 200 provenance, post (attribution, data_origin), narration,<br/>ingest (with lineage), decisions, bias
    UI->>UI: mapAuditResponse() → steps
  end
  UI-->>Reader: receipt: ingestion step, sentiment, relevance, discourse, bias layers

  Reader->>UI: pick an audience
  Note over UI: Public → public · Journalist → plain ·<br/>Regulator → config · Researcher → researcher<br/>(the researcher view names npm run replay -- --post id)
  UI-->>Reader: the same steps in that audience's words
  opt API or network failure on a live post
    UI-->>Reader: an error state, a live receipt is never fabricated
  end
